stack ADT can be implemented morethan one way undermeath
*Arra-based - bacled by a plain array (or ArrayList) //No shifts (Contiguos)
*Linked-list based - backed by a chain of nodes //Scattered (pointers)

Both satisfy the stack ADT, - push/pop/peek behave identically from the outside
But their performance characteristics differ. 
Array-based stacks have O(1) time complexity for push and pop operations, but may require resizing when the array is full.
Linked-list based stacks have O(1) time complexity for push and pop operations as well, 
but they use more memory due to the storage of node pointers.


